 N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"34ad4cce72b7231394abb490d466e8e95f0eb0a9f8dfa270237353973cb8f573","compact":"36cc471c81e30df101f24d0daa42961c5203040ecff8c5577984633f2609872b","nasal":"ebb80337d929b730caf862127914f887a9ed3109fb5717a6e211379d8eb94e98"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-106-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":106,"verse":20,"english":"Why do I not hear as formerly the solemn sounds of song and instrumental music spreading on all sides in Ayodhyā?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.794,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-114-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2106020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"99921b790c674bd6e321a90db235d0183574853839c73332e395e565f7e5b245","compact":"62ab91b91436a9c69c50d8a9d14c2d37721ac942baf615a399041cc6b8dcd375","nasal":"b2855039f1b2ce1c99f8ddcd8df121d37549d4fbd968582d7e1397e4b040febb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-106-21","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":106,"verse":21,"english":"And there does not breathe around the aroma of liquor, or the perfume of garlands, or the incense of aguru and sandal.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.583,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-114-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2106021","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d270f3c59cde9c46fea20e0aa565303dbe5cc3fb0ffa4d558e9309e6474d8a47","compact":"9216fc82eecee457ea4cff0be243e3fe48173dc43666531a3c7b5870747c3b6c","nasal":"27bf95167447697074c5d21f9850e4bd560431eeedd67f40eded7d3795e0faa2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-106-22","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":106,"verse":22,"english":"And on Rāma being banished, in this city is not heard the mild neighing of steeds, the rattle of vehicles, the roar of mad elephants, or the mighty clatter of arms. And on Rāma having repaired to the forest, youthful folk stricken with sorrow do not enjoy the incense of aguru and sandal, or costly fresh chaplets. And persons bearing variegated garlands do not walk abroad; and no festivities are celebrated in the city stricken with grief on account of Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.443,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-114-19","DUTT-2-114-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2106022","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aebd180cabee270d24bfc7284ca25251b4a571e95491569a602db03d3680f776","compact":"47bc39de34857d615ed323901f13bd9079a71d95a9b84bb926741b544f821ca3","nasal":"47bc39de34857d615ed323901f13bd9079a71d95a9b84bb926741b544f821ca3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-106-23","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":106,"verse":23,"english":"And the highways shall be graced with young people elegantly attired and bearing themselves bravely in Ayodhyā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.721,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-114-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2106023","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c3ab4c6218fb2f8af7ca180cf052ca5f6c41bacdbd20f8ed1d9cb02e6cfce059","compact":"354b49cca1f262760256c1c18675eb7eabec908fc0958262676175d0ee0290ff","nasal":"db3dc8b250d1ab2de52055c4789325a3c152496924bd5ceaccd929ecb3d05459"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-106-24","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":106,"verse":24,"english":"Having said this in grief, Bharata in company with the charioteer entered Ayodhyā and immediately went to the residence of his father, bereft of that foremost of men, like a cavern bereft of its lion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.724,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-114-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2106024","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ca5d44c5e65867cb2d86402820f5b96c93aabce5357e2e9